{
  "_": "Finished renders shown on Phiegg's home page. app/phiegg/scripts/home-pictures.py reads this: each picture is a render with a clear ground, set whole on a card of `ratio` (the figure with `margin` of the card's height above and below), `height` pixels tall, written to public/<out>/<name>.webp. {DL} is the Downloads folder. The home page reads the list it shows from src/data/landing.json (ask.fan), not from here. `group` holds further sets, each with its own source, out folder and shape: `cut` (the default) crops to the figure and sets it on a card of `ratio`; `whole` keeps the picture as it is, only made `height` tall at most. The home page shows the sets named in landing.json (gallery), the About page those in about.json. The folder's interface-inspo pictures are other people's screens, kept as reference only and never written out.",
